# Demo knowledge pack - relation vocabulary (lesson 00)
#
# This file teaches the relations BY EXAMPLE. The relations you introduce
# here define which questions become askable later (the "frame").
#
# Sentence form: SUBJECT VERB OBJECT  (one per line, # starts a comment).
# Multi-word verbs use underscores (is_part_of).
#
# is a        -> class membership (taxonomy)
# causes      -> causality (transitive: A->B, B->C => A->C)
# is_part_of  -> part-whole (transitive)
# shows       -> property / observation
# resembles   -> similarity / analogy

Socrates is a human
A human is a mammal
A mammal is an animal
Water causes erosion
Erosion is_part_of weathering
A heart is_part_of a body
Fire shows heat
A dog resembles a wolf
